{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":2,"timestamp":1786539069,"nonce":"9LHylL5MmvGa4ykrG8uxquh9ZTE=","title":"`notification/service.links` builds three Alertmanager UI deep links from `base_url` with no source-kind guard","was":"**What is wrong.** `ViewService.links` builds three Alertmanager UI URLs by concatenating stock Alertmanager paths onto `snap.Group.AlertmanagerURL`, and it never asks what kind of source that URL came from. `internal/notification/service/view.go:402-410` trims the trailing slash and writes `base + \"/#/alerts?filter=\"` (`:405`), `base + \"/#/silences/new?filter=\"` (`:406`) and `base + \"/#/alerts\"` (`:408`). `AlertmanagerURL` is the source's `base_url` verbatim — `internal/notification/domain/snapshot.go:89-92` says so (\"AlertmanagerURL is the source's `base_url`. It is what the Silence and \\\"Open in Alertmanager\\\" deep links are built from (§H.3, R3)\"), and `groupFactsSQL` in `internal/notification/repository/snapshot.go:49-58` selects `coalesce(s.base_url,'')` at `:54` through `LEFT JOIN alert_sources s ON s.id = g.source_id` at `:57`. That join reads one column and stops; `s.kind` is never selected, so the kind is not merely unconsulted — it is not in the snapshot at all."}]}